From 7cd0804e70dff104b86ba6cbd62f53fbf67b4166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:25:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/92] ggml, moe-stream : later prefill waves write their down
 GEMM in place instead of being summed

With the pairs of other waves skipped, every pair belongs to exactly one wave, so the waves fill disjoint
rows of the down output. ggml_mul_mat_id_into (new, CUDA only) is ggml_mul_mat_id with dst a view of an
accumulator and op_params[2] = 2: the CUDA path then skips the memset that op_params[2] = 1 does and
leaves the rows of skipped pairs as they are. The first wave zeroes as before, every later wave writes into
its output, and the per-wave ggml_add over the whole ubatch is gone: a prefill profile at -ub 1024 put it
at 25% of the GPU time (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.25).

DeepSeek V4.1-Flash Q2mix, prompts of 2159 / 8897 tokens, tok/s: -ub 2048 124 / 156 -> 129 / 164,
-ub 1024 85 / 103 -> 88 / 110. MUL_MAT_ID 877/877; KL against the -ub 512 io-1 reference unchanged:
mean 0, max 5.8e-5, same top-1 100%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
